The newest entry is not necessarily the best way into the work. A [2017 post about information architecture](/posts/20170723-corporate-design-through-ia.html) leads more naturally to a [2026 argument about content delivery](/posts/20260327-content-architecture-shipping-container/) than to whatever happened to be published between them. A [type experiment from 2018](/posts/20180319-data-font-for-life-sciences.html) makes more sense beside later work on [data fonts](/posts/20260512-datatype-data-font-inside-out/) and [embedded SVG text](/posts/20260429-svgomg-font/).

The [Corpus Story Lab](/stats/story-lab/) tests those readings. One view looks for ideas that return after several years. Another view assembles "biographies" from a few editorial anchor posts and the entries closest to them in meaning.

